{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"7517655439b8ca9759c61715c6770a7486e09406415e36a9a41f70669e009ab5","slug":"chapters.preface.what-is-programming","location":"/chapters/preface/what_is_programming.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Was ist Programmieren?","numbering":{"title":{"enabled":true,"offset":1},"equation":{"enabled":true,"continue":true},"heading_1":{"enabled":false},"heading_2":{"enabled":false},"heading_3":{"enabled":false},"heading_4":{"enabled":false},"heading_5":{"enabled":false},"heading_6":{"enabled":false}},"content_includes_title":false,"keywords":["python","chemistry"],"thumbnail":"/python_for_chemists/build/computer_figma-acaf5480d1e0e53a0835bbe55485c554.pdf","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"what_is_programming.md","url":"/python_for_chemists/build/what_is_programming-3af09796e49b66017686ac56a018050b.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","kind":"caution","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under Construction","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"B7BUSPCFGK"}],"key":"uUWW8ePVy5"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Diese Seite befindet sich noch im Aufbau. Bitte haben Sie etwas Geduld, bis sie vollständig ist.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"mcGWIPMwbU"}],"key":"Eovyxs6VLe"}],"key":"LiFUXQyIrp"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Programmieren bedeutet, einem Computer Anweisungen so aufzuschreiben, dass er sie Schritt für Schritt ausführen kann. Diese Anweisungen werden in einer Textdatei gespeichert und bilden zusammen ein Programm.","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"ShPOEbN0vS"}],"key":"RErRmtn0lv"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ein Computer verarbeitet Informationen nach festen Regeln. Er “versteht” nicht, was wir meinen, sondern führt nur genau die Befehle aus, die ihm gegeben werden.","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"F2t7GSFM5a"}],"key":"swdJ9NcKce"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Python ist eine Programmiersprache, also eine bestimmte Art, solche Anweisungen zu formulieren. Sie ist gut lesbar und deshalb besonders geeignet, um die Grundlagen des Programmierens zu lernen.","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"qEGL44rH3b"}],"key":"OaX5FDOizQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wenn Sie ein Python-Programm starten, liest der Computer den Code und arbeitet die Befehle der Reihe nach ab. So lassen sich Berechnungen automatisieren, Daten auswerten und wiederholbare Abläufe zuverlässig ausführen.","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"gazpVZUmOd"}],"key":"RAWo4c5AUP"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/python_for_chemists/build/computer_figma-acaf5480d1e0e53a0835bbe55485c554.pdf","align":"center","key":"IyfGgD8sJc","urlSource":"../../assets/figures/preface/computer_figma.pdf"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"k2TXIUL7HH"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/python_for_chemists/build/python_figma-1dca92ae50c3ccf333f83347ddc4b7b3.pdf","align":"center","key":"bqjTg90M7p","urlSource":"../../assets/figures/preface/python_figma.pdf"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"yIhLhnbeOh"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/python_for_chemists/build/code_figma-c70f4844e6e40fe85993a7771d194